drm/omap: claim overlays again for the plane state restored on resume

drm_atomic_helper_suspend() duplicates the plane states, overlay
pointers included, and then disables the planes, which releases their
overlays from the global hwoverlay_to_plane map. On resume the saved
state is committed again: omap_plane_atomic_check() finds an overlay in
the plane state and keeps it without assigning it in the map. The plane
then uses an overlay the map calls free (another plane could get it),
and the next disable warns in omap_overlay_release() (seen on the N810
on the second suspend to RAM). Drop overlay pointers the global state
doesn't map to the plane, so they're assigned again.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/omapdrm/omap_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/omapdrm/omap_plane.c
@@ -221,6 +221,18 @@
 	if (IS_ERR(omap_overlay_global_state))
 		return PTR_ERR(omap_overlay_global_state);
 
+	/*
+	 * The state drm_atomic_helper_resume() restores was duplicated
+	 * before suspend and still names the overlays the plane had then,
+	 * which suspend released from the global map: claim new ones.
+	 */
+	if (omap_state->overlay &&
+	    omap_overlay_global_state->hwoverlay_to_plane[omap_state->overlay->idx] != plane)
+		omap_state->overlay = NULL;
+	if (omap_state->r_overlay &&
+	    omap_overlay_global_state->hwoverlay_to_plane[omap_state->r_overlay->idx] != plane)
+		omap_state->r_overlay = NULL;
+
 	dispc_ovl_get_max_size(priv->dispc, &width, &height);
 	max_width = width << 16;
 	max_height = height << 16;
